<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE shenzhou-24 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-25: T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-25T00:18:52Z (+52 s from the CMSA targeted instant 2026-11-25T00:18:00Z, Beijing 08:18:00). SOURCE CONFLICT: CMSA announced 08:18:00 Beijing (00:18:00Z) via Xinhua and CASC on 24 Nov. LL2 id c9605b67-8a53-4239-a8ae-577fe3b79799, Launch Successful, net 2026-11-25T00:18:52Z, second precision, last_updated 2026-11-25T15:38:41Z. Used LL2. Xinhua English https://english.news.cn/20261125/6d15117da2a3456fa97c351b2bc58931/c.html : Launch of Shenzhou-24 crewed spaceship a complete success. That page gives no clock and does not report docking, so docking is not recorded. utc shifted +52 s. ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. Knots not moved. ILLUSTRATIVE.
CONFIRMED 2026-11-24, no utc shift: T0 2026-11-25T00:18:00Z is the CMSA targeted instant (Beijing 08:18 on 25 Nov), and it already matched the files. Xinhua (https://www.news.cn/20261124/18101736be3f4ef098c062ec82fb2a2a/c.html) and CASC, citing CMSA (https://www.spacechina.com/n25/n2014789/n2014804/c4764137/content.html): crew Tang Hongbo (commander; spacecraft pilot), Wu Yi (flight engineer), Muhammad Zeeshan Ali (Pakistan; payload specialist). After insertion the plan is a 3.5-hour fast autonomous rendezvous, docking at the Tianhe forward port. Instantaneous: the LL2 window 00:08-00:48Z is not the clock used here. LL2 id c9605b67-8a53-4239-a8ae-577fe3b79799 re-queried this run: still Go, net 2026-11-25T00:18:00Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-20T09:07:56Z, no result. ECEF unchanged. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2F/G Shenzhou-24 (Jiuquan LA-91 / SLS-1) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 12.00 s, kick 1.446 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 7840 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.7320-0.002377*(t-t_ign stage 2).
Vehicle config: Long March 2F/G (crewed, escape tower not in the mass) (sim/vehicles/lm2fg.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-2F/G TIMELINE mode. Hard event times are Baidu encyclopedia&#x27;s theoretical crewed sequence (booster 154.8 s, S1 cutoff 159 s, separation 159.5 s, fairing 212.5 s, S2 main 463.1 s, vernier 582.1 s). CMSA Shenzhou-5 (137/159/200/460/587 s) and CMSA Shenzhou-14 (about 577 s) are recorded on the launch file and are not these hard times.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. Shenzhou-24, Long March 2F/G, Jiuquan Launch Area 91 / SLS-1 (921), crewed flight to Tiangong. T0 is the LL2 NET 2026-11-25T00:18:00Z, status Go, window 00:08-00:48Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-20T09:07:56Z. https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/c9605b67-8a53-4239-a8ae-577fe3b79799/
TIME CONFLICT, not silent. CMSA and Xinhua have not published a clock time. Xinhua 21 Nov 2026 (English and Chinese) reports the final rehearsal and gives no liftoff time. The CMSA flight-list page still ends at Shenzhou-23. Wikipedia EN lists NET 25 Nov 2026 00:19 UTC and cites Next Spaceflight; the Next Spaceflight page lists 00:18 UTC. 00:19 was not used. 05:18 AM Pakistan Standard Time equals 00:18Z because PKT is UTC+5; no Pakistani post stating 05:18 was retrieved for this file, so that wording is not an independent source.
Azimuth 97.16 deg is the east-southeast supplement for Tiangong&#x27;s published 41.47 deg inclination. No NOTAM or debris notice covering 25 Nov 2026 00:08-00:48Z was found (space-notices ZBPE danger areas checked; the November 5 and November 9 polygons do not cover this window). The 82.84 deg supplement was not used.
Event times are the Baidu encyclopedia theoretical crewed sequence, not a Shenzhou-24 timeline: booster sep 154.8 s, S1 cutoff 159 s, stage sep and S2 ignition 159.5 s, fairing 212.5 s, S2 main cutoff 463.1 s, vernier cutoff 582.1 s, ship separation 585.1 s. Conflicts recorded and not used as the hard times: English Wikipedia rounds the 2F/G booster burn to 153 s (was 140 s). CMSA Shenzhou-5, basic rocket: escape tower 120 s, boosters 137 s, stage sep and S2 ignition 159 s, fairing 200 s, main cutoff 460 s, separation 587 s, orbit 199.14 x 347.8 km at 42.4 deg. CMSA Shenzhou-14: separation about 577 s. Wikipedia Shenzhou profile: about 12 s pitch, 120 s tower at about 40 km, boosters about 152 s, fairing about 205 s, main cutoff about 460 s, separation about 580 s. zh.wikipedia Shenzhou-23 clocks, no footnote on that bullet: liftoff 23:08:36, separation 23:18:21, which is 585 s and matches 585.1 s rather than 577 s. CMSA Shenzhou-23 and Xinhua say only about 10 minutes. The 577 s figure was tried as an exact cutoff and left the published stage-2 load partly unburned with SMA about 218 km short of 200 x 350 km, so the hard times are the theoretical sequence.
Target 200 x 350 km is the CMSA design orbit, not Shenzhou-24&#x27;s elements. Inclination is Tiangong&#x27;s 41.47 deg (Wikipedia infobox, statistics as of 25 Apr 2024), not the 42 deg of Shenzhou-8 or the 42.4 deg of Shenzhou-5, and not the station&#x27;s 386 x 392 km altitude. Payload 7,840 kg is the Wikipedia spacecraft figure, not a Shenzhou-24 weigh-in.
Target (see launch config): insertion 200 km, apoapsis 350 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 97.16 deg; payload 7840 kg.
Pad: 40.957893N 100.290944E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-25T00:18:52Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+582.1 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+585 s; rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+585 s (https://baike.baidu.com/item/%E9%95%BF%E5%BE%81%E4%BA%8C%E5%8F%B7F/53504320): alt 188.46 km, osculating 131.7 x 241.3 km, i 41.78 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Shenzhou-23 CMSA and Xinhua say only that separation was about 10 minutes after liftoff. 577 s and 585.1 s both sit inside that phrase. The file uses 585.1 s.</description>
